WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.240
There are fascinating questions in this video...

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:08.100
For example, is Gael kneeling to the statue behind the altar?

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:12.260
Who is his merciful Goddess of the Forlorn?

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:17.300
And what is the white-haired woman's "Dark Soul of Man"?

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:18.520
Let's see.

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:21.860
The painted world has always been a safe haven,

00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:27.500
in the age of the gods, it was the work of the painter Ariamis, hung in Anor Londo,

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:31.400
and home to beings like Priscilla, whose abilities the gods feared.

00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:35.220
At some point, though, we know that this painting fell,

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:38.860
for Father Ariandel restored the painted world,

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:42.060
and the cycle of paintings began anew.

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:47.740
Of course, there could have been many paintings and painters in between these two worlds

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:48.620
of Ariamis and Ariandel

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:55.420
because the residents of this painting clearly understand that eventually their world must burn,

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:57.820
lest their painting stagnate and rot.

00:00:57.820 --> 00:00:59.820
That's a line of thought that only really comes about

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:02.760
if they've had generations go through this. (BREATHE, VAATI)

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:07.840
And yet, Ariandel decided to eschew tradition,

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:09.340
he embraced rot.

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:10.840
Buried the flame.

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:14.680
And decided instead to satiate the flame with his blood.

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:17.720
And so, the next painter had to be tucked away,

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:23.140
in the depths of the painting. Never to paint the next world, never to see flame.

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:30.880
Tasked with concealing this secret child of the painting, is Vilhelm, loyal knight of Friede,

00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:33.460
who is the tyrant of Ariandel.

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:36.040
"I've seen your kind,

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:38.520
time and time again,"

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:42.320
"Every fleeing man must be caught,

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:44.560
every secret must be unearthed,"

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:49.140
"Such is the is conceit of the self-proclaimed 'Seeker of Truth',"

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:52.320
"But in the end, you lack the stomach,"

00:01:52.940 --> 00:01:55.360
"For the agony that you'll bring upon yourself."

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:58.960
Friede was the first ash to enter the painting,

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:02.300
yet instead of seeking flame, she embraced the rot—

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:04.980
along with the Good Father—and she entrusted

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:07.780
Vilhelm with the key to this library.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:12.420
And within this place are what seem to be secrets of the painting.

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:15.860
As a tyrant, as Friede, you want to hide history,

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:18.040
you want to hide origins,

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:21.620
and I think this place—this library—is where a lot of that is hidden.

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:25.080
Perhaps these books hold the histories of the world?

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:28.740
Maybe the destroyed statues hide an important identity?

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:33.120
And, certainly, Vilhelm guards the white-haired child

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:36.060
who is the key to the future of the next world.

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:38.800
"Forgive me, my lady...

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:41.160
"I swore an oath...

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:43.480
"But I have failed you...

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:48.100
"Lady Elfriede..."

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:51.240
The white-haired woman shares no name,

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:56.980
so we call her "Aria" in keeping with the tradition of painters named this way.

00:02:57.780 --> 00:02:59.140
"I believe...

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:03.020
"I feel the scent of ash upon thee...

00:03:03.020 --> 00:03:05.880
"Thou art the one of whom Uncle Gael spoke...

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:08.760
"The one to show me flame...

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:12.960
"'Tis good... I'll head off to paint...

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:16.140
"I promised Uncle Gael I would..."

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:17.640
Uncle Gael.

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:22.580
The Japanese text actually confirms that she doesn't mean "uncle" in the literal sense,

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:26.940
rather she means "uncle" in the familiar-old-man sense.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:33.240
This is important because the parentage of Aria is something worth going into a bit later.

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:38.160
But for now, let's tackle Gael's curiosities, and he has a ton of them.

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:41.080
"Gael was once a "Slave Knight",

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:45.100
which was a warrior used as fodder in the bleakest of battles.

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:51.220
And perhaps he still is one, because that same description mentions that

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:54.380
slave knights were never relieved from duty.

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:57.800
Despite their twisted bones and blackened skin.

00:03:58.360 --> 00:04:04.040
And, bizarrely, we never actually get a clue as to what a slave knight's duty could be.

00:04:04.420 --> 00:04:09.560
Nor what entity they were beholden to for this duty, as it's called.

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:12.740
Additionally, slave knights were clearly downtrodden,

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:16.440
yet they were given lavish red armaments,

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:19.600
its fine craftsmanship a symbol of honor.

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:27.080
So, I think all of this serves to make us feel like Gael is from a long-lost time,

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:30.740
and one of the oldest undead in the series.

00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:36.460
And this is a thought that's reinforced by the miracle that he alone wields.

00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:40.380
The Way of White Corona is a lost Way of White miracle,

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:43.140
a white discus which slices though foes

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:46.740
and is SO SHIT that it's no wonder people forgot about it. (No, really, it sucks.)

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:50.840
Long ago, when the imprints left by the gods were still deep,

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:55.040
miracles of the Way of White existed alongside "orioles".

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:58.620
These were the white discs that existed in Dark Souls I

00:04:58.620 --> 00:04:59.920
at the age of the gods,

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:03.760
that appeared in other people's worlds whenever you cast a miracle.

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:05.900
The description goes on to say:

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:09.400
"Those who yearned for the long-lost orioles

00:05:09.420 --> 00:05:12.060
fully believed that they would return one day."

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:16.560
You find this Way of White miracle in the Corvian Settlement

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:18.760
in front of their church altar.

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:22.140
And this is an altar that looks stunningly similar

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:25.580
to one on the outside in the Cathedral of the Deep,

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:27.720
which was a church of the Way of White.

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:30.440
And it's this same place where Gael,

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:31.900
the ancient,

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:36.860
duty-bound knight says his next curious line of dialogue:

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:39.720
"Merciful Goddess...

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:41.880
"Mother of the Forlorn...

00:05:42.260 --> 00:05:45.320
"who have no place to call their own...

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:51.180
"Please, bear witness to our resolve...

00:05:51.260 --> 00:05:54.320
"Fire for Ariandel...

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:58.140
"Fire for Ariandel..."

00:05:59.620 --> 00:06:04.180
"And the ash to kindle flame..."

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:07.080
So who is this "merciful Goddess"?

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:09.260
This "Mother of the Forlorn"

00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:11.620
who Gael still believes is watching over them.

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:15.200
Perhaps she's the clue to understanding Gael's motivations?

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:20.720
I'll list three strong candidates, so let me know which one you think is correct.

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:24.380
First: Caitha, the Goddess of Tears.

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:28.420
I came across this suggestion in the comments of a missing dialogue video,

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:29.940
and I love the theory.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:36.080
It drew my attention to the fact that Gael may well be kneeling to the figure behind the altar

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:37.240
in the Cleansing Chapel,

00:06:37.340 --> 00:06:41.820
which is a statue that's repeated all throughout the Cathedral of the Deep.

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:43.900
The woman is clutching her face,

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:45.960
almost as if weeping.

00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:50.500
And this ties in nicely with Caitha, who is the Goddess of Tears,

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:58.520
and who is mentioned in the Blue and Red Tearstone rings as a "mourner of loved ones and of the undeserving dead."

00:06:58.520 --> 00:07:01.820
We don't know too much about her motivations as a goddess, but

00:07:02.280 --> 00:07:06.380
we know that she was famously worshiped by Morne and his archbishop,

00:07:06.540 --> 00:07:08.860
both of whom hail from Carim.

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:11.300
And that's pretty much everything we know.

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:14.940
But additionally, as StellarElite points out in the comments,

00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:18.200
the Cathedral is a former Way of White church,

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:21.800
and the Way of White now has a home in Carim.

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:26.420
And Gael is related to the Way of White, soo you can see the connections here.

00:07:26.700 --> 00:07:31.180
But the real question is: Can she classify as a "merciful Goddess"?

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:33.600
As a "Mother of the Forlorn"?

00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:38.720
Well, followers of Caithe, they provide comfort to the suffering,

00:07:39.660 --> 00:07:45.260
and a Goddess of Tears certainly qualifies her to be a merciful Mother of the Forlorn,

00:07:45.260 --> 00:07:46.280
don't'cha think?

00:07:46.360 --> 00:07:48.200
But the links do stop there.

00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:51.800
And we've never really had a clue as to Caitha's motivations,

00:07:51.800 --> 00:07:56.700
and she certainly doesn't have a relationship with anything in the painted world.

00:07:56.700 --> 00:07:59.720
So, our second candidate: Velka, Goddess of Sin,

00:08:00.380 --> 00:08:01.980
does have a connection.

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:04.060
Instead of a claim through the Way of White,

00:08:04.060 --> 00:08:08.060
Velka instead is more directly related to the painted world.

00:08:08.060 --> 00:08:12.680
For example, in Dark Souls I there was a Black Pardoner set, that was found within

00:08:13.060 --> 00:08:18.580
and the crows were originally envisioned as servants of Velka in the design works,

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:23.380
though it is possible that part of their design has changed.

00:08:23.380 --> 00:08:28.120
But, at any rate, Velka certainly has a relationship with the Sable Church,

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:31.360
and it makes a degree of sense for Velka to be

00:08:31.500 --> 00:08:34.620
invested in the opposite of what Friede wants.

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:38.040
Since Friede was a member of the Sable Church,

00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:39.780
who abandoned the Church.

00:08:40.760 --> 00:08:47.000
There are also destroyed female statues that have loose-fitting robes and one hand outheld.

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:50.740
Which is quite similar to the statue of Velka in the settlement.

00:08:51.340 --> 00:08:54.140
So does Velka fit as a "merciful Goddess"?

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:56.460
As a "Mother of the Forlorn"?

00:08:56.460 --> 00:08:58.300
I think you could see her that way,

00:08:58.360 --> 00:09:03.780
uh, absolving sin is a mercy, and she has a statue for just that,

00:09:03.780 --> 00:09:05.120
tucked away in the Undead Settlement.

00:09:05.380 --> 00:09:10.180
For absolving sin, can you go so far as to call her a Mother of the Forlorn?

00:09:10.180 --> 00:09:16.060
That's more of a stretch, but we really know so little about Velka that you can't rule it out.

00:09:16.440 --> 00:09:19.000
As for the last candidate: Priscilla

00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:22.340
She's certainly not quite classified as a goddess,  but

00:09:22.340 --> 00:09:24.400
she's very much a mother figure,

00:09:24.420 --> 00:09:27.060
and is based in the first painted world.

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:30.420
As such, she likely wouldn't tie in with Gael's

00:09:30.580 --> 00:09:33.800
hollow-slave duties, but at the very least,

00:09:33.940 --> 00:09:38.160
we should discuss Priscilla's relationship with the child, Aria.

00:09:38.600 --> 00:09:41.080
Most notably, Aria's scaled skin...

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:43.820
and her red, slitted eyes...

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:47.080
like Priscilla's green ones, and this quote:

00:09:47.160 --> 00:09:52.040
"Those who aren't kin to fire, cannot paint a world...

00:09:52.620 --> 00:09:54.640
"Those absorbed by fire...

00:09:55.380 --> 00:09:57.780
"Must not... paint a world...

00:09:58.560 --> 00:09:59.680
"Don't worry...

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:02.640
"I haven't forgotten, mother..."

00:10:03.420 --> 00:10:08.580
Admittedly, there have certainly been a lot of paintings between this one and Ariamis,

00:10:08.600 --> 00:10:15.440
so, like so many other things in this video, it's up to you to decide if we can even guess at Aria's parentage,

00:10:15.440 --> 00:10:20.540
or the identity of the so-called "merciful Goddess, Mother of the Forlorn,"

00:10:20.540 --> 00:10:21.820
so what do you think?

00:10:22.060 --> 00:10:23.740
"My thanks, Ashen One...

00:10:24.980 --> 00:10:26.980
"I can almost see the flame...

00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:28.860
"Soon,

00:10:28.860 --> 00:10:31.580
"Uncle Gael will bring me the pigment...

00:10:32.300 --> 00:10:34.220
"I wonder if he has found it?"

00:10:35.240 --> 00:10:36.920
"The Dark Soul of Man..."

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:42.280
The most curious and tantalizing quote at the end of the DLC,

00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:45.700
I feel like it's only fitting that we end the video in the same way.

00:10:46.540 --> 00:10:49.500
Similar to how man can usurp the first flame,

00:10:50.040 --> 00:10:55.320
Aria is also looking to paint the Dark Soul of Man upon her canvas as the pigment,

00:10:55.940 --> 00:10:58.340
though she doesn't have it just yet.

00:10:59.700 --> 00:11:02.020
Gael is out there searching for it.

00:11:02.020 --> 00:11:04.460
Maybe it's the final piece of his duty?

00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:07.320
But where does he intend on finding this?

00:11:07.820 --> 00:11:10.540
What shape does the Dark Soul of Man take?

00:11:10.540 --> 00:11:13.520
Is it as little as a simple humanity fragment,

00:11:13.760 --> 00:11:17.780
or as large as a soul of man akin to the Soul of Cinder?

00:11:17.820 --> 00:11:21.320
As usual we're left with more questions than answers, and

00:11:21.420 --> 00:11:23.340
at the end of the DLC, no less.

00:11:23.800 --> 00:11:28.300
And From aren't exactly known for making sequential DLC's,

00:11:28.840 --> 00:11:31.800
since you can purchase these separately, so

00:11:31.800 --> 00:11:36.660
I have a feeling we're going to be left to figure this out for quite a while to come.

00:11:37.400 --> 00:11:39.660
So, what will the final DLC hold?

